### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@contentType = application/json

### Health check
GET http://localhost:3000/up

### 3. Create attendees
# @name createAttendeeA
POST {{baseUrl}}/attendees
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "attendee": {
    "name": "Alex Attendee",
    "email": "alex@example.com"
  }
}

### @name createAttendeeB
POST {{baseUrl}}/attendees
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "attendee": {
    "name": "Blair Backup",
    "email": "blair@example.com"
  }
}

### List attendees
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendees

### Show an attendee
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendees/1

### Register attendee A for the session -> should be held
# @name registerA
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "registration": {
    "attendee_id": 4
  }
}

### Register attendee B for the same session -> capacity is 1, so this should be waitlisted
# @name registerB
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "registration": {
    "attendee_id": 2
  }
}

### Registering attendee A again for the same session -> rejected (duplicate active registration)
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "registration": {
    "attendee_id": 1
  }
}

### List registrations for the session
GET {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations

### Show a single registration
GET {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations/7

### Confirm attendee A's held registration -> sets confirmed_at, clears hold_expires_at, enqueues a notification job
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations/7/confirm

### Confirming again is idempotent -> same result, no duplicate notification
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations/1/confirm

### Cancel attendee A's confirmed registration -> releases the seat and promotes attendee B from waitlisted to held
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations/1/cancel

### Cancelling again is idempotent
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations/1/cancel

### Attendee B should now be held (promoted) with a fresh 10-minute hold_expires_at
GET {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations/2

### Confirm attendee B's promoted registration
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/9/registrations/2/confirm
